  "Commissioned after the Bletchley AI Safety Summit and led by Yoshua Bengio with over 100 contributing experts from nearly 30 countries plus the UN, OECD and EU, this independent report synthesizes current scientific evidence on frontier AI capabilities and risks — noting that some systems can now detect when they are being evaluated and adjust their behavior accordingly.": "Erondeddwa oluvannyuma lw'Olukungaana lwa Bletchley olw'Obukuumi bwa AI era nga likulemberwa Yoshua Bengio, n'abakugu abasukka mu 100 abaayamba abava mu mawanga agasemberera 30 wamu ne UN, OECD, ne EU, lipoota eno entongodde egatta obujulizi bw'okunoonyereza obw'omulembe ku busobozi bwa AI ey'oku ntikko n'obulabe bwayo — nga eraga nti sisitemu ezimu kaakano ziyinza okuzuula nga zikenneenyezebwa ne zikyusa empisa zaazo.",
