  "Currency": "Ssente",
  "Custom tier": "Omutendera gwo Ggwe",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nous awa lipoota ku kiwandiiko ekyaggyibwa mu magazini Journal of Medical Ethics ekyalimu ensibuko ez'obulimba, eza AI hallucination — nga ne zirimu amayunivaasite ag'obulimba n'endagiriro za email ezitakyaliwo — omuwandiisi gy'ategeezebwa nti teyazikyusa n'oluvannyuma lw'okuweebwa omukisa okuzikyusa. Ekiwandiiko kigeraageranya kino ne Bioethics, ekiweebwa okukebera ensibuko mu makina, ekyandizuudde ekizibu ekyo, era kigamba nti ekizibu ennyo si tekinologiya y'okuzuula (script y'omu ku bawandiise yazuula ensibuko ez'obulimba mu ddakiika ttono), wabula mulimu gw'abakebezi abatasasulwa n'ebisikiriza by'okufulumya ebiwandiiko ebisasula obungi okusinga obulungi.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Okukozesa Data Bwereere n'Omuwendo gwa AI ogw'Obuttiriyoni",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabis yawaayo ekiteeso ky'okubaawo ekibiina eky'okulondoola nga FINRA eri okufulumya emideeli gy'oku ntikko: laabu zandiwaddeyo emideeli okukenneenyezebwa okumala ennaku 30 nga tezinnafulumizibwa, mu kusooka nga kya bwereere, nga waliwo ekkubo okutuuka ku kugoberera okuwalirizibwa mu katale ka US.",
  "Denied": "Kigaanibwa",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Ekifaananyi ky'Okutandika Polisi Ekiyinza Okussibwawo",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Ekifaananyi ky'okutandika polisi ekiyinza okussibwawo kiri ku /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — omukutu omutonotono ogw'omuzingo omujjuvu ogusomeka makina, nga gwetegese eri Cloudflare Pages oba omukutu gwonna omulala.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Okussawo Polisi Ezisomeka Makina ku Mukutu gwo",
  "Disclaimer": "Okwewaawo",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "Nga kyawukana ku UI ey'abantu, SEO, oba API ezitongole, AI Ingestion & Capability Layer ewa emikutu enzimba etunuulidde makina: Omuzingo gwa Manifest (ebifo eby'okuyingira nga /llms.txt ne /ai/manifest.json), Omuzingo gwa Corpus (obumanyi obusomeka makina), Omuzingo gw'Obusobozi (ebikozesebwa AI ez'obwannannyini bye ziyinza okukoowoola), n'Omuzingo gw'Obufuzi (ensibuko, obuyisensi, emyaka). Gutandika nga static, era guyinza okulongoosebwa okutuuka ku API ne MCP. Mumanye: mu mpapula eno AICL etumbula enzimba y'okulya; ku mpapula za protocol ez'omukutu guno AICL etegeeza Omuzingo gw'Obuyisensi bw'Ebirimu bya AI.",
